WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.818 --> 00:00:16.160
Zann could see that Perda was feeling frustrated with Vilkor.

2
00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:21.944
"I don't know why she didn't tell him that we're from Magica, not Terrica," Zann thought.

3
00:00:21.964 --> 00:00:23.685
"But I'm sure she had a good reason."

4
00:00:24.345 --> 00:00:28.608
Perda tried once again to convince Vilkor that he didn't need a well anymore.

5
00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:34.483
Zann decided it was easier to show him how magic worked than to try to explain it.

6
00:00:34.503 --> 00:00:37.705
"Watch this," Zann said.

7
00:00:38.126 --> 00:00:41.328
He rubbed his hands on his legs to create plenty of friction.

8
00:00:42.288 --> 00:00:47.012
Then he used an Enlarging spell to double the size of the pond in front of them.

9
00:00:48.453 --> 00:00:53.496
Next Zann turned the water blue and created a small wooden dock and a rowboat.

10
00:00:54.617 --> 00:00:55.837
He glanced at Vilkor.

11
00:00:56.678 --> 00:00:59.460
The man's jaw had dropped in astonishment.

12
00:01:00.068 --> 00:01:01.629
"How did you do that?"

13
00:01:02.209 --> 00:01:07.312
Vilkor asked, sinking onto a bench as if he didn't trust his legs to hold him upright.

14
00:01:07.332 --> 00:01:09.293
"Easy. I used magic."

15
00:01:09.894 --> 00:01:14.917
Zann rubbed his hands together and then added an elaborate fountain to the middle of the pond.

16
00:01:15.897 --> 00:01:19.319
He shot a look toward Perda, wondering what she thought of his efforts.

17
00:01:19.339 --> 00:01:21.581
"This cannot be happening."

18
00:01:22.501 --> 00:01:24.923
Vilkor glared at Zann suspiciously.

19
00:01:24.943 --> 00:01:27.164
"I must be asleep and dreaming."

20
00:01:28.412 --> 00:01:30.973
Zann added a pretty shrub to the edge of the pond.

21
00:01:30.993 --> 00:01:34.114
"Anyone can do this, now that Terrica has magic."

22
00:01:35.035 --> 00:01:40.057
Thinking about Mellis' failure to create water, he added, "At least we think so.

23
00:01:40.537 --> 00:01:41.457
Why don't you give it a try?"

24
00:01:41.477 --> 00:01:44.999
"Maybe he shouldn't," Perda whispered.

25
00:01:45.019 --> 00:01:52.962
"The magic energy seems kind of unpredictable so far, and besides—" "No, it's fine," Zann assured her.

26
00:01:52.982 --> 00:01:55.363
"I didn't have any trouble with the spells I just did."

27
00:01:55.903 --> 00:01:58.024
He glanced proudly at the lovely pond.

28
00:01:59.164 --> 00:02:01.345
Vilkor stood, looking intrigued.

29
00:02:01.965 --> 00:02:03.166
"What do I need to do?"

30
00:02:03.566 --> 00:02:04.846
he asked cautiously.

31
00:02:05.687 --> 00:02:11.109
Zann quickly explained about friction and focusing words and the other basics of creating items.

32
00:02:11.129 --> 00:02:13.370
"Go ahead," he finished.

33
00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:15.851
"Try to create something, like a glass of water."

34
00:02:17.152 --> 00:02:19.112
Vilkor still looked suspicious.

35
00:02:19.553 --> 00:02:22.934
But he followed Zann's instructions, rubbing his hands together.

36
00:02:22.954 --> 00:02:27.456
"Mmm water," he said.

37
00:02:28.168 --> 00:02:31.010
A rough pottery cup of water appeared in his hand.

38
00:02:31.791 --> 00:02:34.472
The man was so shocked, he nearly dropped it.

39
00:02:34.492 --> 00:02:35.613
"It worked!"

40
00:02:36.093 --> 00:02:37.054
Vilkor exclaimed.

41
00:02:37.074 --> 00:02:38.515
"Can it really be true?

42
00:02:39.075 --> 00:02:41.597
Can I create anything I want?"

43
00:02:42.738 --> 00:02:44.639
"Almost anything," Perda said.

44
00:02:44.659 --> 00:02:47.401
"You can't create people or animals.

45
00:02:48.021 --> 00:02:54.846
And you shouldn't create anything that might hurt others or Vilkor was already rubbing his hands together again.

46
00:02:54.866 --> 00:02:56.807
"Wheel of fine cheese!"

47
00:02:57.287 --> 00:02:57.808
he shouted.

48
00:02:58.216 --> 00:03:01.539
A large chunk of cheese landed with a thump in front of him.

49
00:03:02.279 --> 00:03:07.943
After that, Vilkor created a pair of silk pants for himself, along with a matching hat.

50
00:03:07.963 --> 00:03:12.066
"Oh," he said, looking disappointed.

51
00:03:12.086 --> 00:03:16.089
"I wanted a feather in the hatband, but it's not there."

52
00:03:16.109 --> 00:03:19.772
"Slow down," Zann said with a chuckle.

53
00:03:19.792 --> 00:03:22.774
"You're new to this, and your magic energy might be running low.

54
00:03:23.394 --> 00:03:23.915
Don't worry.

55
00:03:24.175 --> 00:03:25.616
It'll return after a short rest."

56
00:03:26.504 --> 00:03:29.866
He noticed that Perda was watching Mellis and looking worried.

57
00:03:29.886 --> 00:03:32.808
"Mellis still looks pale," Perda said.

58
00:03:32.828 --> 00:03:36.331
"All that magic energy might have made her ill.

59
00:03:37.271 --> 00:03:39.093
Maybe we should take her to see Zira."

60
00:03:39.993 --> 00:03:42.895
"Zira?" Vilkor stopped playing with his new hat.

61
00:03:43.956 --> 00:03:46.438
"No! I don't want her to know what's going on here."

62
00:03:47.178 --> 00:03:47.899
"What do you mean?"

63
00:03:48.279 --> 00:03:48.959
Zann asked.

64
00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:52.482
Vilkor stroked his new silk pants.

65
00:03:52.502 --> 00:03:56.500
"This special magic thing is on my land," he said.

66
00:03:56.520 --> 00:04:03.125
"I don't want anyone else to know about it until I've figured out how best to, er, deal

67
00:04:03.185 --> 00:04:03.505
with it."

68
00:04:03.525 --> 00:04:05.887
"It's okay," Mellis said.

69
00:04:05.907 --> 00:04:07.708
"I'm feeling better already."

70
00:04:07.728 --> 00:04:09.429
"Hear that?

71
00:04:09.809 --> 00:04:10.990
She's fine."

72
00:04:11.571 --> 00:04:13.152
Suddenly Vilkor gasped.

73
00:04:13.632 --> 00:04:14.493
"What is that thing?"

74
00:04:14.893 --> 00:04:15.934
he cried in alarm.

75
00:04:16.554 --> 00:04:20.777
Zann spun around, thinking about the rock trompers Mellis had told them about.

76
00:04:21.237 --> 00:04:25.140
And who knew what other wild, dangerous creatures might be in this world?

77
00:04:25.964 --> 00:04:27.465
But all he saw was Zing.

78
00:04:28.365 --> 00:04:32.748
Until now, the little dragon had been resting in the shade of the flowers that had grown up

79
00:04:32.828 --> 00:04:33.308
around him.

80
00:04:33.929 --> 00:04:37.011
He'd finally stood up and walked to the bank of the pond.

81
00:04:37.031 --> 00:04:42.834
"Oops," Zann whispered, realizing that they'd forgotten to refresh the chupo disguise.

82
00:04:44.155 --> 00:04:46.476
But that was no big deal now, he realized.

83
00:04:47.076 --> 00:04:48.837
He rubbed a hand against his side.

84
00:04:49.438 --> 00:04:52.860
He had no idea what a chupo looked like, but he did his best.

85
00:04:53.344 --> 00:04:58.687
He used a Visual Confusion spell to make Zing look like the mud lizards he and Darb used

86
00:04:58.727 --> 00:05:01.768
to search for in the swamps of Magica when they were little kids.

87
00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:05.089
Vilkor blinked, looking more startled than ever.

88
00:05:05.109 --> 00:05:06.730
"What's happening?"

89
00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:07.511
he said.

90
00:05:08.131 --> 00:05:10.072
Mellis laughed and glanced at Zing.

91
00:05:10.812 --> 00:05:12.433
She really did look stronger now.

92
00:05:13.133 --> 00:05:16.435
The color had returned to her cheeks, and her eyes were bright.

93
00:05:17.155 --> 00:05:18.135
She snapped her fingers.

94
00:05:18.155 --> 00:05:23.523
"Chupo," she whispered just loudly enough for Zann and Perda to hear her.

95
00:05:24.064 --> 00:05:25.965
The Visual Confusion spell shifted.

96
00:05:26.846 --> 00:05:32.951
Now Zing looked brown and furry, with a pair of curved fangs emerging from a blunt snout.

97
00:05:32.971 --> 00:05:34.992
"See, Uncle?"

98
00:05:35.393 --> 00:05:35.933
Mellis said.

99
00:05:35.953 --> 00:05:37.675
"It's just a chupo.

100
00:05:38.515 --> 00:05:41.638
You're probably a little light-headed from doing all that magic.

101
00:05:42.138 --> 00:05:44.660
It's not surprising if you're imagining things."

102
00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:48.884
"Hmm." Vilkor looked suspicious again.

103
00:05:49.632 --> 00:05:53.836
Just then he noticed a plump purple fruit hanging from a nearby tree.

104
00:05:53.856 --> 00:05:56.338
"Would you look at that!"

105
00:05:56.758 --> 00:05:57.418
he exclaimed.

106
00:05:57.438 --> 00:06:00.061
"I thought that tree would never bear fruit.

107
00:06:00.761 --> 00:06:02.763
And the fruit is so large!

108
00:06:03.663 --> 00:06:08.788
I can charge a premium for those at the village market He was still muttering with delight as

109
00:06:08.828 --> 00:06:10.489
he rushed over to pick the fruit.

110
00:06:10.509 --> 00:06:14.973
"Are you sure you don't want to see Zira, just in case?"

111
00:06:15.393 --> 00:06:16.514
Perda asked Mellis.

112
00:06:17.775 --> 00:06:18.836
Mellis shook her head.

113
00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:22.142
"I'm feeling better and better," she said.

114
00:06:22.162 --> 00:06:27.507
"Besides, I don't really trust Zira—or her right-hand man, either."

115
00:06:28.547 --> 00:06:30.489
Zann wasn't sure what she meant by that.

116
00:06:31.089 --> 00:06:34.112
Before he could ask, though, Zira strode into view.

117
00:06:34.132 --> 00:06:37.575
"What in Terrica is going on here?"

118
00:06:38.035 --> 00:06:38.556
she asked.
